"To calculate the required rate of return for SmileWhite using the CAPM formula, we use the following equation:\n\n\\[ \\text{Required Rate of Return} = \\text{Risk-Free Rate} + \\beta \\times (\\text{Expected Market Return} - \\text{Risk-Free Rate}) \\]\n\nFor SmileWhite:\n- Beta (\\(\\beta\\)): 1.15\n- Risk-Free Rate: 4.50%\n- Expected Market Return: 14.50%\n\nPlug these values into the formula:\n\n\\[ \\text{Required Rate of Return} = 4.50\\% + 1.15 \\times (14.50\\% - 4.50\\%) \\]\n\n\\[ \\text{Required Rate of Return} = 4.50\\% + 1.15 \\times 10\\% \\]\n\n\\[ \\text{Required Rate of Return} = 4.50\\% + 11.50\\% \\]\n\n\\[ \\text{Required Rate of Return} = 16.00\\% \\]\n\nTherefore, the required rate of return for SmileWhite is 16%.\n\nANSWER: C."
