"To calculate the punching shear bearing capacity \\( F_l \\) of the cushion cap, we use the following approach:\n\n1. **Determine Perimeter of Critical Section:**\n\n   The critical section perimeter is calculated at a distance \\( d = h_0 = 1050 \\text{ mm} = 1.05 \\text{ m} \\) from the column face.\n\n   The column section size is \\( 0.6 \\, \\text{m} \\times 0.6 \\, \\text{m} \\).\n\n   Therefore, the critical section perimeter (\\( u \\)) is:\n   \\[\n   u = 4 \\times (0.6 + 2 \\times 1.05) = 2.4 + 8.4 = 10.8 \\text{ m}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate Design Punching Shear Capacity:**\n\n   The punching shear capacity is given by:\n   \\[\n   V_c = u \\times d \\times f_t\n   \\]\n   where:\n   - \\( u = 10.8 \\text{ m} \\) (perimeter of critical section)\n   - \\( d = 1.05 \\text{ m} \\) (effective depth)\n   - \\( f_t = 1.27 \\text{ MPa} \\) (tensile strength design value)\n\n   Substitute the values:\n   \\[\n   V_c = 10.8 \\times 1.05 \\times 1.27 = 14.3781 \\text{ MPa} \\cdot \\text{m}^2\n   \\]\n\n3. **Convert to kN:**\n\n   Since \\( 1 \\text{ MPa} = 1 \\text{ N/mm}^2 = 1000 \\text{ kN/m}^2 \\), convert \\( V_c \\) to kN:\n   \\[\n   V_c = 14.3781 \\times 1000 = 14378.1 \\text{ kN}\n   \\]\n\nThe punching shear bearing capacity \\( F_l \\) of the cushion cap is 14378.1 kN.\n\nANSWER: A. "
