"To determine which U.S. foreign policy is illustrated by the cartoon, we can analyze the components:\n\n1. **Domino Theory:** The title \"Domino Theory\" is central to the image, a concept that was prominent during the Cold War. It suggested that if one country in a region came under the influence of communism, then surrounding countries would follow in a domino effect.\n\n2. **Presidential Figures:** The dominoes are labeled with the names of U.S. Presidents (Ike, JFK, LBJ, Nixon, Ford) who were involved in Cold War-era policies, particularly in Southeast Asia.\n\n3. **Context of the Era:** During the 20th century, a primary focus of U.S. foreign policy was to prevent the spread of communism, especially during the Vietnam War\u2014an application of the Domino Theory.\n\nGiven this context, the image most directly supports the idea of \"stopping the spread of communism in Asia.\"\n\nANSWER: A."
