"To allocate joint costs using the net realizable value (NRV) method, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate Net Realizable Value (NRV) for each product:**\n\n   - NRV = Total Final Sales Value - Separable Costs\n\n   - Product M: \n     \\[\n     NRV = \\$160,000 - \\$10,000 = \\$150,000\n     \\]\n\n   - Product N: \n     \\[\n     NRV = \\$140,000 - \\$10,000 = \\$130,000\n     \\]\n\n   - Product T: \n     \\[\n     NRV = \\$25,000 - \\$5,000 = \\$20,000\n     \\]\n\n2. **Calculate total NRV:**\n\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total NRV} = \\$150,000 + \\$130,000 + \\$20,000 = \\$300,000\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the proportion of NRV for each product:**\n\n   - Product M: \n     \\[\n     \\text{Proportion} = \\frac{\\$150,000}{\\$300,000} = 0.5\n     \\]\n\n   - Product N: \n     \\[\n     \\text{Proportion} = \\frac{\\$130,000}{\\$300,000} \\approx 0.4333\n     \\]\n\n   - Product T: \n     \\[\n     \\text{Proportion} = \\frac{\\$20,000}{\\$300,000} \\approx 0.0667\n     \\]\n\n4. **Allocate joint costs based on these proportions:**\n\n   - Product M: \n     \\[\n     \\text{Joint Cost Allocation} = 0.5 \\times \\$120,000 = \\$60,000\n     \\]\n\n   - Product N: \n     \\[\n     \\text{Joint Cost Allocation} = 0.4333 \\times \\$120,000 = \\$51,996\n     \\]\n\n   - Product T: \n     \\[\n     \\text{Joint Cost Allocation} = 0.0667 \\times \\$120,000 = \\$8,004\n     \\]\n\nBased on the calculations, the correct choice is:\n\nANSWER: C."
