"To calculate the Mean Square Factor (MSF), we first need to go through the following steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the group means**:\n   - Group 1 Mean: \\((216 + 198 + 240 + 187 + 176) / 5 = 203.4\\)\n   - Group 2 Mean: \\((202 + 213 + 284 + 228 + 210) / 5 = 227.4\\)\n   - Group 3 Mean: \\((170 + 165 + 182 + 197 + 201) / 5 = 183.0\\)\n\n2. **Calculate the overall mean**:\n   - Overall Mean: \\((203.4 + 227.4 + 183.0) / 3 = 204.6\\)\n\n3. **Calculate the Sum of Squares for the Factor (SSF)**:\n   - SSF = \\(5 \\times ((203.4 - 204.6)^2 + (227.4 - 204.6)^2 + (183.0 - 204.6)^2)\\)\n   - SSF = \\(5 \\times ((-1.2)^2 + (22.8)^2 + (-21.6)^2)\\)\n   - SSF = \\(5 \\times (1.44 + 519.84 + 466.56)\\)\n   - SSF = \\(5 \\times 987.84 = 4,939.2\\)\n\n4. **Calculate the Mean Square Factor (MSF)**:\n   - MSF = SSF / (number of groups - 1)\n   - MSF = \\(4939.2 / 2 = 2,469.6\\)\n\nANSWER: D."
