"To find the probability that a randomly selected hit was made by Babe Ruth, use the formula for probability:\n\n\\[ P(\\text{event}) = \\frac{\\text{Number of favorable outcomes}}{\\text{Total number of possible outcomes}} \\]\n\nIn this case:\n\n- Number of favorable outcomes (hits made by Babe Ruth) = 2,873\n- Total number of possible outcomes (total hits) = 12,351\n\nSo the probability is:\n\n\\[ P(\\text{hit was made by Babe Ruth}) = \\frac{2,873}{12,351} \\]\n\nThus, the correct option is B.\n\nANSWER: B"
