"To solve the problem, let's go through the calculations step-by-step.\n\n### (a) Calculate the kinetic energy in the system:\n\n1. **Kinetic Energy of the Mass:**\n   \\[\n   KE_{\\text{mass}} = \\frac{1}{2} m v^2 = \\frac{1}{2} (1000 \\, \\text{kg}) (4 \\, \\text{m/s})^2 = 8000 \\, \\text{J}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Kinetic Energy of the Drum:**\n   - Mass of the drum: \n     \\[\n     m_{\\text{drum}} = \\frac{2.5 \\, \\text{kN}}{9.81 \\, \\text{m/s}^2} = 254.84 \\, \\text{kg}\n     \\]\n   - Angular velocity (\\(\\omega\\)):\n     \\[\n     \\omega = \\frac{v}{r} = \\frac{4 \\, \\text{m/s}}{0.275 \\, \\text{m}} = 14.55 \\, \\text{rad/s}\n     \\]\n   - Moment of inertia (\\(I\\)): \n     \\[\n     I = m_{\\text{drum}} k^2 = 254.84 \\, \\text{kg} \\times (0.25 \\, \\text{m})^2 = 15.9275 \\, \\text{kg} \\cdot \\text{m}^2\n     \\]\n   - Kinetic energy:\n     \\[\n     KE_{\\text{drum}} = \\frac{1}{2} I \\omega^2 = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 15.9275 \\, \\text{kg} \\cdot \\text{m}^2 \\times (14.55 \\, \\text{rad/s})^2 = 1673 \\, \\text{J}\n     \\]\n\n3. **Total Kinetic Energy:**\n   \\[\n   KE_{\\text{total}} = KE_{\\text{mass}} + KE_{\\text{drum}} = 8000 \\, \\text{J} + 1673 \\, \\text{J} = 9673 \\, \\text{J}\n   \\]\n\n### (b) Calculate the additional brake torque:\n\nTo calculate the additional torque required, consider the deceleration needed to stop the system in 0.60 s.\n\n1. **Calculate Deceleration (\\(a\\)):**\n   \\[\n   v = u + at \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad 0 = 4 \\, \\text{m/s} + a \\cdot 0.60 \\, \\text{s} \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad a = -\\frac{4}{0.60} = -6.67 \\, \\text{m/s}^2\n   \\]\n\n2. **Torque due to Deceleration for the Mass:**\n   \\[\n   T_{\\text{mass}} = m \\cdot a \\cdot r = 1000 \\, \\text{kg} \\cdot 6.67 \\, \\text{m/s}^2 \\cdot 0.275 \\, \\text{m} = 1834.25 \\, \\text{N} \\cdot \\text{m}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Torque due to Deceleration of the Drum:**\n   \\[\n   \\alpha = \\frac{a}{r} = \\frac{6.67 \\, \\text{m/s}^2}{0.275 \\, \\text{m}} = 24.25 \\, \\text{rad/s}^2\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   T_{\\text{drum}} = I \\alpha = 15.9275 \\, \\text{kg} \\cdot \\text{m}^2 \\cdot 24.25 \\, \\text{rad/s}^2 = 386.75 \\, \\text{N} \\cdot \\text{m}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Total Additional Brake Torque:**\n   \\[\n   T_{\\text{total}} = T_{\\text{mass}} + T_{\\text{drum}} = 1834.25 \\, \\text{N} \\cdot \\text{m} + 386.75 \\, \\text{N} \\cdot \\text{m} = 2221 \\, \\text{N} \\cdot \\text{m}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Additional Required Brake Torque:**\n   \\[\n   T_{\\text{additional}} = T_{\\text{total}} - T_{\\text{initial}} = 2221 \\, \\text{N} \\cdot \\text{m} - 2698 \\, \\text{N} \\cdot \\text{m} = -477 \\, \\text{N} \\cdot \\text{m}\n   \\]\n   This negative value indicates that the applied torque is larger than needed, hence the additional required torque to bring it to rest is \\(|-477 + 2698| = 2218 \\, \\text{N} \\cdot \\text{m}\\).\n\n### Conclusion:\nBased on these calculations, the correct option is:\n\n**ANSWER: A**"
