"To determine the maximum shortening of the spring due to the impact of the block, we can use the conservation of energy principle. The potential energy of the block at the initial height will be converted into the elastic potential energy stored in the spring at maximum compression.\n\n1. **Initial Potential Energy (PE_initial)**:\n   \\[\n   \\text{PE_initial} = mgh\n   \\]\n   Here, \\( mg = W = 5.0 \\, \\text{N} \\) and \\( h = 200 \\, \\text{mm} = 0.2 \\, \\text{m} \\).\n   \\[\n   \\text{PE_initial} = 5.0 \\times 0.2 = 1.0 \\, \\text{J}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Elastic Potential Energy at Maximum Compression (PE_spring)**:\n   \\[\n   \\text{PE_spring} = \\frac{1}{2} k x^2\n   \\]\n   where \\( k = 90 \\, \\text{N/m} \\) and \\( x \\) is the maximum compression of the spring.\n\n3. **Energy Conservation**:\n   \\[\n   \\text{PE_initial} = \\text{PE_spring}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   1.0 = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 90 \\times x^2\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   1.0 = 45x^2\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   x^2 = \\frac{1.0}{45}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   x = \\sqrt{\\frac{1.0}{45}} = \\sqrt{0.0222} \\approx 0.149 \\, \\text{m} = 149 \\, \\text{mm}\n   \\]\n\nSince \\( x = 149 \\, \\text{mm} \\), and assuming maximum compression as maximum potential shortening:\n\nTotal shortening is 149-mm due to the block falling onto the spring. To find the overall shortening, we will account for the compression only once the block fully compresses the spring by comparing calculated compression with the options provided. \n\nChecking each option:\n- A. 114.64mm \u2014 Doesn\u2019t match calculated shortening, x = 149mm.\n- B. 214.64mm \u2014 Doesn\u2019t match calculated shortening, x = 149mm.\n- C. 314.64mm \u2014 Doesn\u2019t match calculated shortening, x = 149mm.\n  \nUpon further inspection, it seems that maximum potential compression was overlooked. Given typical rounding, the closest matching value would be a typographical error, closest matching maximal physic theoretical values, in order to verify such 114 or 214.64 will account for solution providence which should be examined of question intent.\n\nSo you must conclude:\nANSWER: A"
