"To determine if the equation is correct, we need to analyze the decomposition reaction of ammonium carbonate \\((\\text{NH}_4)_2\\text{CO}_3\\).\n\n**Given Reaction:**\n\\[\n(\\text{NH}_4)_2\\text{CO}_3 \\xrightarrow{\\Delta} \\text{H}_2\\text{O} + \\text{CO}_2 + 2\\text{NH}_3\n\\]\n\n**Steps for Validation:**\n\n1. **Identify the Reactants and Products:**\n   - Reactant: Ammonium Carbonate \\((\\text{NH}_4)_2\\text{CO}_3\\)\n   - Products: Water (\\(\\text{H}_2\\text{O}\\)), Carbon Dioxide (\\(\\text{CO}_2\\)), and Ammonia (\\(\\text{NH}_3\\))\n\n2. **Verify the Balanced Equation:**\n   - **Number of Atoms in Reactants:**\n     - Nitrogen (N): 2\n     - Hydrogen (H): 8\n     - Carbon (C): 1\n     - Oxygen (O): 3\n\n   - **Number of Atoms in Products:**\n     - Water (\\(\\text{H}_2\\text{O}\\)): 2 Hydrogen, 1 Oxygen\n     - Carbon Dioxide (\\(\\text{CO}_2\\)): 1 Carbon, 2 Oxygen\n     - Ammonia (\\(\\text{2NH}_3\\)): 2 Nitrogen, 6 Hydrogen\n\n   - **Product Totals:**\n     - Nitrogen (N): 2 (from 2NH3)\n     - Hydrogen (H): 8 (6 from 2NH3 + 2 from H2O)\n     - Carbon (C): 1\n     - Oxygen (O): 3 (2 from CO2 + 1 from H2O)\n\n3. **Balanced Check:**\n   - The number of each type of atom on both sides of the equation is equal:\n     - Nitrogen, Hydrogen, Carbon, and Oxygen atom counts are consistent.\n\n**Conclusion:** The reaction is indeed balanced.\n\nANSWER: A. True."
