"To determine the missing quantities and percent yields, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Compound A to Compound B**:\n   - Given: 10.0 mol A\n   - Yield: 40.0%\n   - Calculated: 10.0 mol \u00d7 0.40 = 4.0 mol B\n\n2. **Compound B to Compound C**:\n   - Given: 4.0 mol B\n   - Yield: ?\n   - Result: 2.0 mol C\n   - Calculate the yield: (2.0 mol / 4.0 mol) \u00d7 100 = 50.0%\n\n3. **Compound C to Compound D**:\n   - Given: 2.0 mol C\n   - Yield: 25.0%\n   - Calculate moles of D: 2.0 mol \u00d7 0.25 = 0.50 mol D\n\n4. **Compound D to Compound E**:\n   - Given: 0.50 mol D\n   - Yield: 10.0%\n   - Calculate moles of E: 0.50 mol \u00d7 0.10 = 0.050 mol E\n\n5. **Compound E to Compound F**:\n   - Given: 0.050 mol E\n   - Result: 0.0100 mol F\n   - Calculate the yield: (0.0100 mol / 0.050 mol) \u00d7 100 = 20.0%\n\nPutting it all together, the missing values are:\n- Yield B to C: 50.0%\n- Moles of D: 0.50 mol\n- Moles of E: 0.050 mol\n- Yield E to F: 20.0%\n\nThese match the choices in option D.\n\nANSWER: D"
