"To find the coefficient of determination (\\( R^2 \\)), you can use the formula:\n\n\\[\nR^2 = \\frac{\\text{SS back}}{\\text{SS total}}\n\\]\n\nwhere:\n- \\( \\text{SS back} = 1044.352 \\)\n- \\( \\text{SS total} = 1878.400 \\)\n\nPlugging these values into the formula gives:\n\n\\[\nR^2 = \\frac{1044.352}{1878.400} \\approx 0.556\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the coefficient of determination is approximately 0.556.\n\nANSWER: B. 0.556"
"To calculate the attributable risk (AR), we use the formula:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Attributable Risk (AR)} = \\text{Incidence in Exposed Group} - \\text{Incidence in Non-Exposed Group}\n\\]\n\nFrom the table:\n\n- Incidence in the exposure group = 58/100,000\n- Incidence in the non-exposed group = 5/100,000\n\nSubstitute the values into the formula:\n\n\\[\n\\text{AR} = 58 - 5 = 53/100,000\n\\]\n\nThus, the attributable risk is 53.0 per 100,000.\n\nANSWER: B"
