"To calculate the incidence of the disease in 2010, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Count the number of new cases**: Look at the graph and count the number of occurrences represented by circles (onset), which appear between 2010/1 and 2010/11. \n\n2. **Calculate Incidence**: \n   \\[\n   \\text{Incidence} = \\left(\\frac{\\text{Number of new cases}}{\\text{Population at risk}}\\right) \\times 100\n   \\]\n\n3. **Data Extraction**:\n   - New cases in 2010: Count the circles from the graph. There are 8 new cases.\n\n4. **Apply the formula**:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Incidence} = \\left(\\frac{8}{2528}\\right) \\times 100 \\approx 0.316\\%\n   \\]\n\n5. **Select the correct option**: Based on the approximate incidence percentage:\n\n   ANSWER: C. 0.32%."
